From f1413742e5b3108fd37fcafa67c6f169402bea3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:42:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/32] (b) v2, part b-3: replaced \@caption: settings until
 the next caption

For \caption* the kernel let \fnum@<type> be the empty label and made
\addcontentsline a no-op only while a replaced \@caption ran (classes
such as llncs, mwcls, jpsj2). Reviews of round 1 found (F2, N2, N5):

- mwcls with hyperref makes its own target in \@caption with
  \hyper@makecurrent and the unchanged \theH<type>: \caption* and
  continued captions got a second destination with the name of the
  last stepped caption ("destination with the same identifier"), and
  \ref led to that caption.
- A replaced \@caption that defers its work (llncs + threeparttable,
  caption above the table) ran after the settings were undone: "Table
  1." with the previous number and the list entry "1 Starred above".
- In the kernel \@caption the \par came before the restore, so the
  paragraph hooks (and the output routine for \captionof*) saw the
  changed definitions.

Now \@caption@nostep@defs prepares a caption that does not step its
counter: \theH<type> gets the unique suffix *<n> (so a target that a
replaced \@caption makes has a new name), and for \caption* also
\fnum@<type> is \@caption@nolabel and \ext@<type> is empty, so that
\addcontentsline writes to no list. \addcontentsline itself is no
longer changed, so an \addcontentsline{lof}... right after \caption*
works. The settings are local and last until \@caption@nostep@restore:
at the start of the kernel \@caption (before the \par), at the start of
the next \caption, or at the end of the group, which covers a deferred
\@caption as well. \@caption is again the last token of \caption*, so
float's optional argument after the caption works. The kernel \@caption
gives the number of the unused suffix back, so the kernel path has no
gaps in the names (figure.1*1, figure.1*2). This replaces \@caption@star.

Tests: caption-interface-001 tests 21-23 show the new settings; new
tests: a replaced \@caption that makes its own target (unique names for
\caption* and a continued caption, a manual \addcontentsline after
\caption* is written, settings undone by the next \caption and at the
end of the float), a replaced \@caption that defers (no label, no list
entry), and no gap in the names on the kernel path. float-024: the same
with hyperref's real plugs and an mwcls-like \@caption, no duplicate
destination.

Matrix (pdfLaTeX, 182 documents: 10 classes x 9 modes, the H3 and mwcls
documents of the round-1 verification and the review's documents),
previous head against this commit: llncs + threeparttable no longer
prints "Table 1." and no longer writes "1 Starred above" (also tagged);
duplicate destinations with mwcls and hyperref go from 6/7/12 to 2/3/4
(metahyp/nopatch/taghyp; TL: 5/7/10) and \caption* gives none; the
remaining ones come from mwcls making a target for stepped captions
outside floats, as with TL. Other changes are names of unique targets.
